course: dictionary
lesson: 8415
title: Many meanings of running
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings. «Running» is a good example. Its meaning depends on the words around it, so you use context to find the right one. Look for clues in the sentence first.
explain: Running can mean moving fast on your feet, as in «The sign says "No running in the corridor".» It can also mean the sport itself: «Running keeps you fit.» Here the word names an activity, not an action.
explain: Running can mean flowing or working too. «Never stand behind a car with its engine running» means the engine is switched on and working. A check you can use: swap in a new meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Running is the -ing form of the verb run: run, runs, ran, run, running.
fact: «Running» can be a verb, a noun or an adjective, so check how it is used in the sentence.
fact: «Running water» means water that is flowing, like in a river or a tap. In science, running water carries soil and shapes rivers.
fact: «Three days running» means three days in a row, one after another.
fact: «Running late» means you are behind time, and «a running nose» means a nose that is dripping.
exercise: «The sign says "No running in the corridor".» What does running mean here? | Flowing like water | *Moving fast on your feet | Working or operating | Managing a shop
exercise: «Never stand behind a car with its engine running.» What does running mean here? | *Working or operating | Flowing like a river | Moving fast on your feet | In a row, one after another
exercise: Science tells us that running water carries soil and shapes rivers. What does running mean in running water? | Winning a race | Sleeping | *Flowing | Moving fast on your feet
test: «It rained three days running.» What does running mean here? | Working or operating | Flowing | Moving fast on your feet | *In a row, one after another
test: «Running keeps you fit.» In this sentence, what is running? | *The sport or activity of running | Moving fast on your feet | Water flowing downhill | A machine that is switched on
exam: «Mia is running a shop.» What does running mean here? | Flowing like a stream | Moving fast on your feet | *Managing | Sleeping
